(function () {
  window.DENO_DOC_SEARCH_INDEX = {"kind":"search","nodes":[{"id":"namespace_explainfailure","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"explainFailure","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Explains a failure that only surfaced once the package was imported.A run reaches import() only when discovery vouched for the coder, or when discovery was unavailable and the name was taken on trust; either way the package can still turn out to be unloadable, or the export can still fail to behave. This runs the listing after the fact and answers with the same guidance an incomplete invocation would have given, falling back to the raw error when neither the package nor the coder is at fault — a malformed input, say.An UnverifiedArityError is answered without running the listing. It is raised only on the trusted path, where discovery has already failed once, and asking again buys nothing but a second wait — up to another thirty seconds of it when the first attempt timed out.The guides it renders carry no header: the caller announced the specifier before the run started, and repeating it makes every failure open with the same line twice.","url":"./cli.ts/~/explainFailure.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_main","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"main","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Main CLI entry point.Plans the invocation with planCli, then carries it out: announces the resolved specifier and any inferred coder on stderr, then either writes the planned text to its stream and exits with its code, or runs the command. A run that throws is explained through explainFailure and exits 1.","url":"./cli.ts/~/main.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_parsecliargs","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"parseCliArgs","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Parses command line arguments into the three positionals and the flags.Positionals fill the package, coder and command slots in order, skipping any slot a flag already filled — so -p png -c pngFile decode and png pngFile decode mean the same thing. decode and encode are reserved in the coder slot: a second word that names a command is the command, and the coder is left to be inferred (ADR 0005).Every slot is text: positionals are read as strings, so 007 stays 007 rather than becoming the number 7 on its way to the specifier resolver.A blank word fills its slot, and is then refused on its own terms. It used to be dropped as if it had never been typed, which is not a smaller version of the same thing: binstruct \"\" decode slid decode into the package slot and answered confidently about jsr:@binstruct/decode, and -p \"\" did it too. That is the shift an unknown flag causes, arriving by another route, and it takes the same answer — the slots it landed in are named in CliOptions.blankSlots and nothing runs.There is no fourth slot, and a word that reaches for one is refused. Extra positionals used to be dropped where they stood, so binstruct arp arpData decode input.bin — the < forgotten — waited on a terminal for input that was sitting in the file it had just discarded. They are collected in CliOptions.extraArgs instead.A word starting with - is a flag, and -- is how you say it is not. Everything after the separator fills a slot whatever it starts with, so binstruct -- -dash/mod.ts decode names a module the shell tab-completed from a directory called -dash. Without it, -dash/ was read as the flag cluster -d -a -s -h, whose h set --help — and the CLI answered a decode with the whole help screen on stdout, at exit 0, which is precisely the redirect corruption ADR 0001 exists to prevent.A flag that is not recognised is refused, never ignored. Only the five declared here exist; anything else consumes a word and shifts every positional behind it, so binstruct --format json png would have answered confidently about json. They are collected rather than thrown, since reporting them is planCli's job.","url":"./cli.ts/~/parseCliArgs.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_plancli","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"planCli","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Works out what an invocation amounts to, without performing it.A complete invocation becomes a run plan; anything short of one becomes a print plan carrying the guidance for the missing word — on stderr with exit 1, or on stdout with exit 0 under --help. Guidance that reports a failure rather than a missing word stays on stderr either way.An argument the parser could not use is refused before anything else is read, --help and --version included: an unrecognised flag, a blank word, a word past the third slot. The first two shift what the package is — the flag by swallowing the next word, the blank by having been dropped — and the third used to disappear without a word. Answering confidently about a package nobody named, or about bytes that never arrived, is the defect class this whole module is built to avoid.A local package argument is inspected before any of that, and a directory is refused — see directoryGuide. Everything downstream may therefore assume the specifier names one module, which is what lets discovery and import() be handed the same string.Every path validates the coder through discovery first, including a complete one: see chooseCoder for why the shortcut had to go.","url":"./cli.ts/~/planCli.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"I","kind":"Interface","title":"Interface"}],"name":"CliOptions","file":"cli.ts","doc":"CLI configuration options.Every positional is optional, because every prefix of the argument list is a valid invocation; a missing value is undefined and makes the run incomplete rather than invalid.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.package","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Package specifier as typed, before resolveSpecifier.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.package.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.coder","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Coder name, absent when it is to be inferred or asked for.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.coder.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.command","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Command word, absent when it is to be asked for.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.command.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.help","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Print guidance to stdout and exit 0 instead of to stderr and exit 1.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.help.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.version","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Print version information.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.version.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.docs","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Print deno doc output for the chosen coder instead of running it.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.docs.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.unknownFlags","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Flags the parser was given and does not know, as typed.Not an aside: an unrecognised flag consumes a word, so the positionals behind it shift and a different word becomes the package. Nothing runs while this is non-empty.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.unknownFlags.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.blankSlots","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Slots filled with a word that says nothing, named as <package> and so on.A blank argument is still an argument. Dropping it made the words after it mean something else — binstruct \"\" decode read decode as the package — which is the shift an unknown flag causes, by another route. Nothing runs while this is non-empty.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.blankSlots.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_clioptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"CliOptions.extraArgs","file":"cli.ts","doc":"Positionals beyond the third, as typed.There are three slots and no fourth. A word past them was discarded in silence, so binstruct arp arpData decode input.bin — a forgotten < — sat reading a terminal with nothing to say it had ignored the file.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliOptions.extraArgs.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_cliplan","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"CliPlan","file":"cli.ts","doc":"What an invocation amounts to, once its arguments are understood.Splitting the decision from its effects is what makes the guidance testable: every disclosure level, every error path and --help produce a print plan whose text, stream and exit code can be asserted without a process.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CliPlan.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_commandname","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"CommandName","file":"cli.ts","doc":"A command the CLI can carry out.","url":"./cli.ts/~/CommandName.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_commands","kind":[{"char":"v","kind":"Variable","title":"Variable"}],"name":"COMMANDS","file":"cli.ts","doc":"The commands, which are also reserved words in the second positional.","url":"./cli.ts/~/COMMANDS.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_nearestname","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"nearestName","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Picks the candidate closest to a misspelling, for a \"did you mean\" line.Comparison is case-insensitive, so pngfile finds pngFile, and a candidate only counts as close when it is within roughly a third of the typed word in edits — otherwise nothing is suggested rather than something misleading. Ties go to the earliest candidate.A word that is already among the candidates is not a misspelling of anything, and gets no suggestion. It reads as one otherwise: a listed package that would not load answered cannot read jsr:@binstruct/bencode … did you mean bencode?, correcting the user's spelling to the spelling they had used. The guard is exact-match on the word as typed rather than a zero-distance one, because a distance of zero is also what makes pngfile find pngFile, which is worth keeping.","url":"./mod.ts/~/nearestName.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_renderguide","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"renderGuide","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Renders a guidance screen.Blocks are separated by a blank line and the result carries no trailing newline, so the caller can hand it straight to console.error or console.log. The function is pure — the same Guide always renders the same string — which is what lets the disclosure levels, the error paths and --help be tested without a process.","url":"./mod.ts/~/renderGuide.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"Guide","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Everything one guidance screen says.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.header","file":"mod.ts","doc":"First line, echoing the resolved specifier so shorthand is never invisible.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.header.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.diagnostic","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Whether the screen reports a failure rather than disclosing the next word.A pure disclosure level is guidance: --help may relocate it to stdout and exit 0. A diagnostic — an unreadable package, a misspelled coder, a listing that could not be produced — is a failure that happens to be explained well, and stays on stderr with a non-zero exit whatever the flags say, so that binstruct nosuchpkg --help > out.txt cannot report success.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.diagnostic.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.notes","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Lines shown before NEXT: what went wrong, or what was inferred.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.notes.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.next","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The missing word.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.next.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.options","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The values that word may take.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.options.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.try","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Paste-ready commands one step further along.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.try.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guide","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"Guide.footer","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Trailing lines, e.g. the usage recap --help adds.","url":"./mod.ts/~/Guide.footer.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guidenext","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"GuideNext","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The missing word and what it means.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideNext.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guidenext","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideNext.word","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The word, written as it appears in the usage line, e.g. <coder>.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideNext.word.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guidenext","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideNext.meaning","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One line on what the word selects.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideNext.meaning.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoption","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"GuideOption","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One legal value of the missing word.A listing of bare names — the package list of level 0 — sets neither GuideOption.detail nor GuideOption.summary, and is flowed into columns instead of one row per name.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOption.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoption","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOption.name","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The word to type, e.g. png, pngFile or decode.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOption.name.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoption","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOption.detail","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Short annotation shown in its own column, e.g. → PngFile.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOption.detail.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoption","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOption.summary","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One-line description, e.g. the first line of the coder's JSDoc.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOption.summary.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoptions","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"GuideOptions","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The options block: every value the missing word may take.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOptions.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOptions.heading","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Block heading, e.g. PACKAGES or CODERS in png.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOptions.heading.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOptions.items","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The legal values, in the order they should be shown.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOptions.items.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_guideoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"GuideOptions.empty","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Line shown in place of an empty list, e.g. why discovery found nothing.","url":"./mod.ts/~/GuideOptions.empty.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_diagnoseemptydiscovery","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"diagnoseEmptyDiscovery","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Explains why a package yielded no coders, by reading its module graph.Runs deno info --json --quiet <specifier> and reports whether anything in the graph resolves to @hertzg/binstruct. Per ADR 0002 this is not part of the happy path: call it only after discoverCoders succeeded with an empty coders list, since it rebuilds the graph a second time and answers nothing a non-empty discovery has not already answered.deno info exits 0 even when it could not resolve the root, reporting the problem as an error on the offending module instead. A graph carrying one was never walked, so it is a graph-incomplete failure rather than evidence that the package is not binstruct-based — the two are indistinguishable from the module list alone, and the confident verdict is the wrong one.","url":"./mod.ts/~/diagnoseEmptyDiscovery.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discovercoders","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"discoverCoders","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Discovers the coder factories a package exposes, without importing it.Runs deno doc --json --quiet <specifier> and reads the result with readDocSurface. Requires permission to spawn deno (--allow-run=deno); without it the outcome is a permission-denied ToolFailure and callers should fall back to asking for an explicit coder name.A cold lookup pays for building the module graph — on the order of a second for a JSR package — while a warm one is near-instant. One that answers nothing at all is killed after TOOL_TIMEOUT and comes back as a timed-out ToolFailure, so the CLI cannot be left waiting on a subprocess that never speaks.The specifier must name a single module; callers refuse a directory first (./target.ts).","url":"./mod.ts/~/discoverCoders.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_readdocsurface","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"readDocSurface","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Reads a package's discoverable surface out of parsed deno doc --json output.This is the whole of the JSON-shape knowledge, kept pure so it can be tested against captured fixtures without a subprocess. A symbol counts as a coder factory when it is declared as a function whose return type renders as Coder — a string match, per ADR 0002, so a coder hidden behind a type alias that renders as something else is invisible here.Coders that take no required arguments are listed first, because those are the ones the CLI can invoke on the user's behalf (ADR 0005). Declaration order is preserved within each group.The single node is read without choosing between nodes, which is sound only because the specifier named one module: a directory, whose output holds one node per file under it, never reaches here (./target.ts, ADR 0004).Zero nodes is a successful discovery of nothing, not an impossibility. deno doc exits 0 with an empty nodes map for a directory holding no module files, and this destructured Object.entries(doc.nodes)[0] unguarded, so the answer to \"what does this expose?\" was an uncaught TypeError with a stack trace through the CLI's own frames. An empty surface is what the caller already knows how to answer — the \"exposes no coders\" screen — so that is what it returns.","url":"./mod.ts/~/readDocSurface.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_readsymboldocs","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"readSymbolDocs","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Returns deno doc's formatted documentation for one exported symbol.Backs the --docs flag. Formatting is delegated to deno doc rather than reimplemented, so the output matches what the user would see running the tool themselves — including the module doc that --filter prints as a preamble.The positional form deno doc <specifier> <Symbol> is not used: it treats the symbol as a file path and fails for jsr: specifiers, so --filter is the only working spelling.The subprocess colours its output whether or not it is talking to a terminal, and it is talking to a pipe here by construction. The colour decision is therefore taken from this process's stdout, so --docs > notes.txt writes plain text while --docs on a terminal stays readable.","url":"./mod.ts/~/readSymbolDocs.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A single declaration of an exported symbol in deno doc --json output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.kind","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Declaration kind, e.g. function, variable, interface.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.kind.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.location","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Where the declaration lives; the version rides along for JSR specifiers.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.location.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.location.filename","file":"mod.ts","doc":"","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.location.filename.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.jsDoc","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The declaration's JSDoc, when it has one.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.jsDoc.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.jsDoc.doc","file":"mod.ts","doc":"","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.jsDoc.doc.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.def","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Kind-specific detail; for functions, the signature.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.def.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.def.params","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Declared parameters, in order.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.def.params.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocdeclaration","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocDeclaration.def.returnType","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Declared or inferred return type.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocDeclaration.def.returnType.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocjson","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocJson","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The deno doc --json document, narrowed to the parts discovery reads.A specifier that names one module produces exactly one entry under nodes, keyed by the module deno doc resolved — the specifier itself for a registry one. A directory produces one entry per module file found under it, which is why directories are refused before discovery runs.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocJson.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocjson","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocJson.nodes","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One entry per documented module, keyed by the module's own URL.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocJson.nodes.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocnode","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocNode","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A module entry in deno doc --json output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocNode.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocnode","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocNode.module_doc","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The @module JSDoc of the documented module.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocNode.module_doc.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocnode","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocNode.module_doc.doc","file":"mod.ts","doc":"","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocNode.module_doc.doc.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocnode","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocNode.symbols","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Every exported symbol, in declaration order.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocNode.symbols.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocparam","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocParam","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A parameter of a declaration in deno doc --json output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocParam.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocparam","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocParam.kind","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Binding form: identifier, assign, rest, object or array.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocParam.kind.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocparam","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocParam.optional","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Whether the parameter was declared with a trailing ?.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocParam.optional.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocsymbol","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocSymbol","file":"mod.ts","doc":"An exported symbol in deno doc --json output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocSymbol.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocsymbol","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocSymbol.name","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The exported name.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocSymbol.name.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodocsymbol","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocSymbol.declarations","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One entry per declaration, e.g. one per overload.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocSymbol.declarations.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodoctype","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DenoDocType","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A type reference in deno doc --json output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocType.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodoctype","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocType.repr","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Rendered type name, e.g. Coder. Absent for anonymous forms like unions.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocType.repr.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodoctype","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocType.value","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Resolved details, including the type arguments of a generic reference.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocType.value.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_denodoctype","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DenoDocType.value.typeParams","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Type arguments, so typeParams[0] is the T of Coder<T>.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DenoDocType.value.typeParams.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveredcoder","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DiscoveredCoder","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A coder factory found in a package's public types.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveredCoder.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveredcoder","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DiscoveredCoder.name","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The exported name, e.g. pngFile.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveredCoder.name.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveredcoder","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DiscoveredCoder.decodedType","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The T of Coder<T>, absent when it is an anonymous type such as a union.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveredCoder.decodedType.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveredcoder","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DiscoveredCoder.summary","file":"mod.ts","doc":"First line of the factory's JSDoc, absent when it is undocumented.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveredCoder.summary.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveredcoder","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"DiscoveredCoder.requiredParams","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Arguments the caller must supply; 0 means the CLI can call it directly.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveredCoder.requiredParams.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoveryoutcome","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DiscoveryOutcome","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The result of discoverCoders.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoveryOutcome.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_discoverysuccess","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"DiscoverySuccess","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A package whose type declarations were read successfully.coders may still be empty — a package that exposes none is a successful discovery with nothing to offer, not a failure. Feed that case to diagnoseEmptyDiscovery to find out why.","url":"./mod.ts/~/DiscoverySuccess.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_emptydiscoverydiagnosis","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"EmptyDiscoveryDiagnosis","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The result of diagnoseEmptyDiscovery.","url":"./mod.ts/~/EmptyDiscoveryDiagnosis.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_packagesurface","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"PackageSurface","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The public surface of a package as read from its type declarations.","url":"./mod.ts/~/PackageSurface.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_packagesurface","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"PackageSurface.version","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Resolved version, when the specifier resolved to a JSR package.","url":"./mod.ts/~/PackageSurface.version.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_packagesurface","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"PackageSurface.summary","file":"mod.ts","doc":"First line of the module JSDoc, absent when the module is undocumented.","url":"./mod.ts/~/PackageSurface.summary.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_packagesurface","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"PackageSurface.coders","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Coder factories, zero-required-parameter ones first.","url":"./mod.ts/~/PackageSurface.coders.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_symboldocsoutcome","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"SymbolDocsOutcome","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The result of readSymbolDocs.","url":"./mod.ts/~/SymbolDocsOutcome.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ToolFailure","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A deno subprocess that did not produce usable output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.ok","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Discriminant: this outcome carries no result.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.ok.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.reason","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Which environmental condition stopped the tool.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.reason.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.specifier","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The specifier discovery was asked about.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.specifier.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.command","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The argument vector, for a reproducible line in an error message.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.command.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.code","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Exit status, absent when the process never started.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.code.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailure","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ToolFailure.stderr","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The subprocess's stderr, or the message of the error that replaced it.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailure.stderr.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_toolfailurereason","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ToolFailureReason","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Why a deno subprocess spawned by discovery produced no usable output.permission-denied — the CLI was run without --allow-run=deno. Decoding and encoding still work; only discovery is unavailable.not-spawned — the process could not be started at all, e.g. no deno on PATH.minimum-dependency-age — the requested version is younger than the consuming project's minimumDependencyAge, so the graph refused to resolve. Nothing about the invocation was wrong.exited-non-zero — anything else the tool rejected: unknown package, network failure, syntax error in a local entrypoint.graph-incomplete — the tool succeeded, but the module graph it printed carries an error, so it was never walked. deno info exits 0 in this case, which would otherwise read as a graph that simply contains nothing.timed-out — the tool said nothing for TOOL_TIMEOUT and was killed. A stalled fetch inside deno doc has no deadline of its own, so without this the CLI waits forever with a blank screen.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ToolFailureReason.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_ismodulepath","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"isModulePath","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Reports whether a name ends in an extension the runtime will load.Shared by classification here and by the directory listing in ./target.ts, so \"what counts as a module\" is answered in one place: a directory refusal that offered names the classifier would then reject would be teaching a form the tool does not accept.","url":"./mod.ts/~/isModulePath.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvespecifier","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"resolveSpecifier","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Resolves a user-typed package argument to a module specifier.Version suffixes ride along unchanged, so wav@0.2.0 becomes jsr:@binstruct/wav@0.2.0. Bare-name resolution is unconditional: there is no registry lookup and no fallback to another scope, so xhb resolves to jsr:@binstruct/xhb and fails at load time rather than finding @hertzg/xhb.A path is anchored to the working directory and returned as a file:// URL, so that discovery and import() — which disagree about what a relative specifier is relative to — resolve it to the same module. Reading Deno.cwd() is the one thing this function needs from outside its argument, and only for that form.Whether the path names a file or a directory is left open. Both are the \"path\" form, because a directory and the module inside it are indistinguishable as strings and file:///abs/pkg is as much a directory as ./pkg is; the CLI settles the question by stat'ing the resolved target (inspectLocalTarget in ./target.ts). pkg/, ./pkg and /abs/pkg therefore anchor to one URL and reach one decision — resolve normalizes the trailing slash away.","url":"./mod.ts/~/resolveSpecifier.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_shortenspecifier","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"shortenSpecifier","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Renders the shortest form of a specifier that still resolves back to it.The CLI echoes the resolved specifier once, as a header, and uses this short form everywhere else — in listings and in the paste-ready TRY lines — since the shorthand only helps if the tool teaches it. Each candidate is classified and expanded again before it is offered, so a shortening that would be read back as something else (a path, say) is never proposed.","url":"./mod.ts/~/shortenSpecifier.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"I","kind":"Interface","title":"Interface"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier","file":"mod.ts","doc":"A user-typed package argument and everything derived from it.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier.input","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The argument exactly as the user typed it.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.input.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier.specifier","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The module specifier to hand to deno doc.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.specifier.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier.short","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The shortest form that resolves back to ResolvedSpecifier.specifier, for listings and TRY lines. Equal to shortenSpecifier(specifier), except for a path, where it is the input itself — a path is anchored to the working directory the CLI was started in, and only the typed form still says so.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.short.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier.form","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The resolution rule that matched.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.form.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_resolvedspecifier","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ResolvedSpecifier.shorthand","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Whether the input was shorthand, and therefore expanded.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ResolvedSpecifier.shorthand.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_specifierform","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"SpecifierForm","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Which resolution rule matched an input.\"scheme\" — the input opened with one of MODULE_SCHEMES (jsr:, npm:, http:, https:, file:). A colon that is not one of those is just a character in a name or a path.\"scoped\" — the input named a scope and package, without a scheme.\"path\" — the input pointed somewhere on disk: it held a / without being scoped, or began with ., or ended in a module extension. A file and a directory are the same form: which one it is cannot be read off the spelling, and nothing here goes looking. Nor is the form the place to ask — file:///abs/pkg is a \"scheme\" and names a directory all the same.\"bare\" — the input named a package only.\"scheme\" and \"path\" are explicit forms and pass through untouched; \"scoped\" and \"bare\" are shorthand and get expanded.","url":"./mod.ts/~/SpecifierForm.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_inspectlocaltarget","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"inspectLocalTarget","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Reports what a resolved specifier points at, before anything is run on it.Called once per invocation, ahead of discovery, so that a directory is refused before deno doc gets a chance to answer about a module nobody asked about. A non-file: specifier is \"elsewhere\" and touches no filesystem.Every way of failing to answer is a LocalTarget, including a file: specifier that will not parse as a URL: binstruct \"file://a b/x\" used to escape as an uncaught TypeError and a stack trace, because the URL was decoded outside the try that guards the stat.","url":"./mod.ts/~/inspectLocalTarget.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_localtarget","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"LocalTarget","file":"mod.ts","doc":"What sits at the far end of a resolved specifier.\"elsewhere\" — not on this machine (jsr:, npm:, https:), so there is nothing to stat and the runtime resolves it.\"module\" — a file, which is what a package argument has to name.\"directory\" — refused, with LocalTarget.modules offered as the candidates to name instead.\"missing\" — nothing is there at all, which is a different mistake from naming a directory and gets a different message.\"unreadable\" — the target could not be inspected: read permission was denied, or the file: specifier does not parse as a URL and so names no path to inspect at all. Refused rather than assumed to be a module: assuming is how the directory case produced confident wrong output.","url":"./mod.ts/~/LocalTarget.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_listscopepackages","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"listScopePackages","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Lists the packages of the @binstruct scope, live from JSR.The answer is cached under the OS cache directory for a day, so repeated invocations cost one request between them and an offline run that has listed before still gets a list. When the request fails an expired cache is used in preference to nothing, and when there is no cache either the result is an empty list carrying the reason — never an exception, so the caller can always fall back to explaining the shorthand rule instead of a listing.","url":"./mod.ts/~/listScopePackages.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_readscopelisting","kind":[{"char":"f","kind":"Function","title":"Function"}],"name":"readScopeListing","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Reads a package listing out of a parsed JSR scope-packages response.This is the whole of the response-shape knowledge, kept pure so the network path and the cache file can share it and so it can be tested without either. An entry without a usable name is dropped, a missing description becomes the empty string, and the CLI's own package is never a member. The result is sorted by name, because the order the API returns is not part of its contract.An entry with no latestVersion is dropped, because it is a reserved name and not a package: JSR answers the scope listing with every name that has been claimed, published or not. @binstruct/bencode is the standing example — latestVersion: null, versionCount: 0, https://jsr.io/@binstruct/bencode/meta.json 404 — and offering it at level 0 would put a name on the screen that binstruct bencode cannot load, which is the one thing a suggestion list must not do.The cache file is written in this same shape, so a hand-edited or truncated cache is rejected by the same rules as a bad response, and a cached listing carries the versions that got its entries past this filter.","url":"./mod.ts/~/readScopeListing.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_listingsource","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ListingSource","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Where the packages of a ScopeListing came from.network — freshly fetched from JSR.cache — a cached listing still inside its TTL; no request was made.stale-cache — the request failed and an expired cache answered instead.none — nothing was available; packages is empty.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ListingSource.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelisting","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ScopeListing","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The result of listScopePackages.packages is empty only when source is none, and reason is present exactly when something went wrong — on stale-cache it says why the refresh failed, on none it says why there is no list at all.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListing.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelisting","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListing.packages","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The scope's published packages, sorted by name, without @binstruct/cli.Every entry names something jsr:@binstruct/<name> resolves to; reserved names with no version behind them are not members.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListing.packages.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelisting","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListing.source","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Where they came from.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListing.source.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelisting","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListing.reason","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Why the network answer is missing, when it is.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListing.reason.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelistingoptions","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ScopeListingOptions","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Options for listScopePackages.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListingOptions.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelistingoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListingOptions.cacheDir","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Directory holding the cache file. Absent means the OS cache directory; null disables the cache in both directions.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListingOptions.cacheDir.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelistingoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListingOptions.now","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Current time in milliseconds, for ageing the cache.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListingOptions.now.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopelistingoptions","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopeListingOptions.ttl","file":"mod.ts","doc":"How long a cached listing is served before a refetch, in milliseconds.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopeListingOptions.ttl.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopepackage","kind":[{"char":"T","kind":"TypeAlias","title":"Type Alias"}],"name":"ScopePackage","file":"mod.ts","doc":"One published package of the scope, as JSR describes it.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopePackage.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopepackage","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopePackage.name","file":"mod.ts","doc":"Short name, e.g. png; prefix @binstruct/ for the JSR coordinate.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopePackage.name.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopepackage","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopePackage.description","file":"mod.ts","doc":"JSR's one-paragraph description, empty when the package has none.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopePackage.description.html","deprecated":false},{"id":"namespace_scopepackage","kind":[{"char":"p","kind":"Property","title":"Property"}],"name":"ScopePackage.latestVersion","file":"mod.ts","doc":"The version a bare jsr:@binstruct/<name> resolves to today.Never absent: an entry without one is a reserved name rather than a package, and is dropped by readScopeListing.","url":"./mod.ts/~/ScopePackage.latestVersion.html","deprecated":false}]};
})()